 "amendments": {
  "items": {
   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the executive law, in relation to a free mobile application established, operated and maintained by the division of veterans' affairs",
    "basePrintNo": "S7894",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S7894-2015",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §353, Exec L",
    "lawSection": "Executive Law",
    "memo": " BILL NUMBER:  S7894\n\n TITLE OF BILL :  An act to amend the executive law, in relation to a\nfree mobile application established, operated and maintained by the\ndivision of veterans' affairs\n\n PURPOSE :\n\nRequires the Division of Veterans' Affairs to establish, operate and\nmaintain a free mobile application.\n\n SUMMARY OF PROVISIONS :\n\nSection 1: Adds subdivision 14-a to section 353 of the executive law.\n\nSection 2: Sets the effective date at immediately.\n\n JUSTIFICATION :\n\nAs the technology changes, it is important that state agencies, such\nas the Division of Veterans' Affairs, keep up to date on methods of\ndelivery of important information to the public. An app will provide\nveterans and their families with accessible material about federal and\nstate Veterans' benefits, programs and services including employment,\nhealthcare and education.\n\n LEGISLATIVE HISTORY :\n\nThis is a new bill.\n\n FISCAL IMPLICATIONS :\n\nMinimal.\n\n EFFECTIVE DATE :\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
